{"object_id":"iteration_02","revision":1,"content_hash":"1da4dfdb3a922d0cde587d264fb10e6c5fdbd5583f68220283d462117df35f8b","source_run_id":"cloud-repair-formal-ar-04","input_refs":[],"unconsumed_metadata":{},"schema_version":"observation.v2","acquisition_id":"iteration_02","candidate_ref":null,"objective_ref":null,"sample_ref":null,"binding":{},"raw_blocks":[],"derived_features":{"legacy_projection":{"iteration_id":"iteration_02","route_id":"route_01","route_title":"Optimization of TiO2/SiO2 Bilayer with Analytical Quarter-Wave Initialization","route_snapshot":{"route_id":"route_01","title":"Optimization of TiO2/SiO2 Bilayer with Analytical Quarter-Wave Initialization","route_kind":"optimize_existing_stack","scientific_hypothesis":"Swapping the layer order to TiO2 (high index) adjacent to air and SiO2 (low index) adjacent to glass, combined with an initialization based on the analytical quarter-wave condition at the spectral center (575 nm), will allow the gradient optimizer to converge to a distinct local minimum with a lower broadband mean reflectance than the SiO2-first configuration found in Round 1.","design_principle":"Impedance matching via a high-to-low index transition (Air->TiO2->SiO2->Glass) often provides a smoother effective index gradient than low-to-high for this specific substrate/incident pair. Initializing near the theoretical single-wavelength optimum ($d = \\λ_c / 4n$) reduces the risk of the optimizer settling in a shallow local minimum far from the physical resonance condition.","proposed_materials":["tio2","sio2"],"proposed_topology":"Air | TiO2 (Layer 1) | SiO2 (Layer 2) | Glass Substrate","design_variables":["thickness_tio2_nm","thickness_sio2_nm"],"soft_objectives":["minimize arithmetic mean power reflectance from 450 nm to 700 nm","achieve mean reflectance below 0.03 as a soft scoring preference"],"manufacturing_considerations":["layer thickness must be between 40 nm and 160 nm","exactly one layer of TiO2 and one layer of SiO2"],"evidence_ids":[],"theory_basis":["Quarter-wave antireflection condition: $n_1 d_1 = n_2 d_2 = \\λ_c/4$ for zero reflectance at a single wavelength.","Effective medium theory suggesting high-index-first ordering may better match the large Air-Glass index jump."],"expected_advantages":["Potential to escape the local minimum found in the SiO2-first topology.","Analytical initialization provides a physically grounded starting point closer to the global optimum."],"known_risks":["The TiO2-first order might yield a higher minimum reflectance due to stronger Fresnel reflections at the first interface if not perfectly tuned.","The quarter-wave thicknesses for 575 nm might fall outside the 40-160 nm bounds or require scaling that distorts the broadband response."],"execution_request_english":"Execute a deterministic TMM optimization for a planar stack: Incident Medium (Air, n=1.0) | Layer 1 (TiO2, n=2.40, lossless) | Layer 2 (SiO2, n=1.46, lossless) | Substrate (Glass, n=1.52, lossless). Constraints: Both layer thicknesses must be between 40 nm and 160 nm. Objective: Minimize the arithmetic mean power reflectance for s-polarized light at normal incidence over the wavelength range 450 nm to 700 nm (5 nm steps). Optimization Settings: Use seed 17, maximum 64 solver evaluations. Initialize the optimizer with the analytical quarter-wave thicknesses for the center wavelength 575 nm: initial_thickness_TiO2 = 575/(4*2.40) nm, initial_thickness_SiO2 = 575/(4*1.46) nm. If these initial values fall outside the [40, 160] nm bounds, clamp them to the nearest bound before starting the optimization run. Report the final optimized thicknesses, the full reflectance spectrum, and the calculated mean reflectance. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization s. wavelength intervals 450-700 nm. soft objectives: minimize arithmetic mean power reflectance from 450 nm to 700 nm; achieve mean reflectance below 0.03 as a soft scoring preference. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the 450 nm to 700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: layer thickness must be between 40 nm and 160 nm; exactly one layer of SiO2 and one layer of TiO2.","priority":1,"parent_route_id":"route_01","revision_reason":"Feedback directive requested swapping the layer order (TiO2 first) and using an analytical quarter-wave initialization at 575 nm to explore a different region of the design space compared to Round 1's SiO2-first random/gradient start."},"compilation_status":"compiled","compilation_rationale":"The request specifies constant indices, overriding registry dispersion. Two layer orders are permitted; Experiment 1 fixes the order TiO2/SiO2 as requested in the primary instruction. Bounds [40, 160] nm are applied. The optimization targets mean reflectance minimization with a soft preference for <0.03. Seed and evaluation limits are mapped to optimizer settings.","compilation_errors":[],"run_status":"completed","physically_valid_candidate_count":4,"best_target_score":0.529945171199669,"best_robustness_score":0.1301872889606422,"selected_candidate_ids":["ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__gradient_thickness__01","ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__gradient_thickness__03"],"failure_categories":[],"experiment_summaries":[{"experiment_id":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt","mode":"optimize","physically_valid_candidate_count":4,"best_target_score":0.529945171199669,"selected_roles":{"best_target_score":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__gradient_thickness__01","most_robust":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__gradient_thickness__01","simplest_fabrication":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__gradient_thickness__01","structurally_distinctive":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__gradient_thickness__03"}}],"candidate_summaries":[{"candidate_id":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt__baseline","experiment_id":"ar_coating_tio2_sio2_opt","target_score":0.5123049347363324,"robustness_score":null,"simplicity_score":0.9756097560975611,"distinctiveness_score":0.10962494198180399,"thicknesses_nm":[59.8958,98.6301],"optimizer_id":null,"objective